 "limits": [
  "The crossed prompt (item) part of each claim-test contrast's SE is omitted: no prompt-level data exist before block A, so none are simulated for the claim test; the df is the seed part's Satterthwaite df (GXB S-3). Its effect on the size is not simulated: V_prompt >= 0 widens the SE but also raises the Satterthwaite df.",
  "The familywise rate is the rate of the U claims: Holm at 5% on the U contrasts, which bounds Phi's U claims (GXB R-10). Phi's adverse O and L words ('worse (O)', 'worse (L)'), which start at gamma x alpha = 0.5% absolute in all (10% of alpha, alpha = 5%), within their own contrasts, are not simulated (GXB R-11 as corrected by R-27)."
